- Progress-scope rule: each `AGENT_PROGRESS.md` records only changes to state inside its own folder. When a nested subfolder carries its own four-file agent contract, this folder logs only the event of creating or removing that nested workspace; all internal changes (scaffolding, design edits, corpus additions, rename cascades, blocker updates) live in the nested `AGENT_PROGRESS.md` and are not duplicated here. The same applies symmetrically: a nested workspace's progress file does not restate parent-scope events.
